SUMMARY: Opening Reception: Listening To The Wild by Teal Collins & Shane
 y Fago
DESCRIPTION:Usher Gallery presents featured artist Teal Collins alongside
  Shaney Fago in an exhibition exploring intuition\, expression\, and conn
 ection. A self-taught visual artist and lifelong recording singer/songwri
 ter and performing musician\, Collins works in acrylic and oil on canvas 
 (some mixed media)\, blending wildlife imagery with abstract florals and 
 expressive color. Her paintings are intended as visual examples of a **pe
 aceful\, restorative view—a soft place to fall—**offering connection to t
 he quieter\, gentler aspects of life within an overstimulating world. In 
 contrast and dialogue\, Shaney Fago’s work focuses on portraiture and mus
 ic\, capturing emotional presence and musical energy through gesture and 
 mood. Together\, the artists create a visual conversation between nature\
 , sound\, and human expression.\n\nThis joint showcase\, "Listening to th
 e Wild\," fuses sweeping West Coast wildlife and landscapes with the high
 -voltage nostalgia of GenX analog culture.\n\nThe evening will feature fi
 ne wine\, local refreshments\, live music by Musiq For The Soul\, and a c
 hance to meet the artists.\n\nRun Dates: June 2\, 2026 – July 12\, 2026\n
 \nOpening Reception: Saturday\, June 13\, 2026\, from 5:00 p.m. – 8:00 p.
 m.
CATEGORIES:Petaluma,live-music,art,openingreception
