SUMMARY: Speaker Series: Conversations with Women Leaders in Our Communit
 y
DESCRIPTION:Lecture 2 - Hormones\, Myths and What Actually Helps\n\n\nDr.
  Laura Kimbro is a retired OB/GYN physician\, women's health educator\, a
 nd speaker with a passion for helping women navigate the perimenopause an
 d menopause transition with knowledge\, vitality and confidence.\n\n\nDra
 wing from decades of medical experience and a deep interest in healthy ag
 ing\, Dr. Kimbro combines a thoughtful blend of medical science and lifes
 tyle medicine to make complex topics understandable and empowering for he
 r participants.\n\n\nHer lectures invite women to better understand the p
 rofound transition of midlife\, not simply as a medical event but as a me
 aningful new chapter. She explores the hormonal changes of the menopause 
 transition\, as well as the long-term health considerations that follow -
  including heart health\, bone health\, cognition\, sleep\, metabolism\, 
 and longevity. To Dr Kimbro\, aging well is about far more than preventin
 g disease - it's about preserving strength\, curiosity\, purpose\, connec
 tion\, and joy.
CATEGORIES:petalumawomansclub,health,petaluma,womenspeakers
